Fix GNU indent saved-comment buffer identification (Savannah bug 64751).

Local Solaris correction; not an accepted upstream patch.
https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?64751
The maintainer's 2025-09-24 NUL-guard example explicitly leaves the
cur_line/buf_ptr buffer-identity problem unresolved.

search_brace() can move a brace ahead of saved comments and reset
save_com.len without reducing the replay buffer's extent. Testing whether
buf_ptr lies within save_com.ptr + save_com.len then misidentifies saved
input as original input. current_column() scans from cur_line in the
original allocation towards buf_ptr in the saved allocation, potentially
reading past the original input. The membership test itself also compares
pointers to unrelated objects.

Use bp_save, the existing saved-input state: both sw_buffer() and the
preprocessor-comment path set it when selecting save_com, and fill_buffer()
clears it when restoring original input. While replaying, save_com.ptr,
buf_ptr and buf_end refer to the same live allocation; save_com.end is
reset, and save_com.len is not the replay bound. Otherwise cur_line and
buf_ptr refer to the original input. Scanning to buf_ptr therefore stays
within its input allocation, independent of allocation order and without
relying on NUL termination. Use the same state for boxed comments.

Preserve the column calculation and saved-comment start-column behavior,
including tab, backspace, form-feed and newline handling.

--- indent-2.2.13/src/code_io.c
+++ indent-2.2.13/src/code_io.c
@@ -143,10 +143,10 @@
     char *p;
     int column;
 
-    /* Use save_com.size here instead of save_com.end, because save_com is
-     * already emptied at this point. */
-  
-    if ((buf_ptr >= save_com.ptr) && (buf_ptr <= save_com.ptr + save_com.len))
+    /* bp_save identifies saved input.  save_com.end has been reset and
+     * save_com.len may have been shortened when moving a brace.  cur_line
+     * still belongs to the original input, so do not use it for replay. */
+    if (bp_save != 0)
     {
         p = save_com.ptr;
         column = save_com.start_column;
--- indent-2.2.13/src/comments.c
+++ indent-2.2.13/src/comments.c
@@ -164,8 +164,8 @@
       line_preamble_length = 0;
       visible_preamble = 0;
 
-      /* If this comment is in the save buffer, trust it's start_column. */
-      if ((buf_ptr >= save_com.ptr) && (buf_ptr <= save_com.ptr + save_com.len))
+      /* If this comment is in the save buffer, trust its start_column. */
+      if (bp_save != 0)
       {
           start_column = save_com.start_column;
       }
